    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0328" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-05T03:00:00+03:00">May 5, 1936—3 a.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—8:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. Your 189<anchor n="27" xml:id="d290-f1"/> and 190. The night has so far been
                    exceptionally calm and if report in your 187 is even approximately correct, we
                        <pb facs="0329" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/> all feel we should not evacuate.
                    British Legation has so far not got in touch with me, but if, after consultation
                    with officer who would presumably accompany convoy, I consider that there is no
                    other alternative I shall not hesitate to act in accordance with your
                    suggestion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
